.TH FBMQ 1 "February 2026" "fbmq 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fbmq \- file-based message queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbmq
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbmq
is a Unix-philosophy message queue where every message is a Markdown file with
RFC 822 headers, every queue is a directory, and atomic
.BR rename (2)
is the sole coordination primitive.
.PP
Messages are human-readable, renderable, greppable, and diffable.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "init " "dir " "[--priority]"
Initialize a new queue with 256 hash-sharded buckets. With
.B --priority
creates priority subdirectories (0-critical, 1-high, 2-normal, 3-low).
.TP
.BI "push " "dir " "[options] [file|-]"
Enqueue a message. Reads Markdown body from
.I file
or stdin. Prints the message ID to stdout.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-priority " " \fIlevel\fR
One of:
.IR critical ,
.IR high ,
.IR normal
(default),
.IR low .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-ttl " " \fIseconds\fR
Time-to-live.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-correlation\-id " " \fIid\fR
Correlation ID for workflow tracing.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tag " " \fItag\fR
Add a tag (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-created\-by " " \fIname\fR
Override default created_by.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-fsync
Skip fsync for tmpfs/RAM-disk mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-batch\-fsync
Defer directory fsyncs. File data is still fsynced (message content is durable),
but the directory entry is not fsynced until
.B fbmq sync
is called. When used with a standalone
.B push
command, sync is called automatically after enqueue.
.RE
.TP
.TP
.BI "sync " "dir"
Flush deferred directory fsyncs for all pending buckets, processing/, and failed/.
Use after a batch of
.B push \-\-batch\-fsync
calls to ensure directory entries are durable. The kernel coalesces these into a
single journal transaction, so one
.B sync
covers all preceding enqueues.
.TP
.BI "pop " "dir"
Claim the next available message. Prints the claimed file path to stdout.
The message is on disk \(em read it with
.BR cat (1)
or
.BR "fbmq cat" .
Exit 0 on success, 1 if empty.
.TP
.BI "ack " "dir path"
Mark a claimed message as done.
.TP
.BI "nack " "dir path"
Return a message for retry. Increments retry_count. Dead-letters after max retries.
.TP
.BI "depth " "dir"
Print queue depth. Scans all 256 pending buckets and processing/ on each call.
Stateless \(em no persistent counter files.
.TP
.BI "reap " "dir " "[-l secs]"
Reclaim stale processing messages and expire TTL-exceeded pending messages.
.TP
.BI "purge " "dir " "[-a secs]"
Delete done messages older than
.I secs
(default: 604800 = 7 days).
.TP
.BI "inspect " "file"
Print parsed metadata from a message file.
.TP
.BI "cat " "file"
Print only the Markdown body (strips frontmatter).
.TP
.B version
Print version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ fbmq init /var/queue/jobs

$ echo "# Deploy v2.1" | fbmq push /var/queue/jobs \-p high
a3f2e1b4c5d6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6

$ CLAIMED=$(fbmq pop /var/queue/jobs)
$ cat "$CLAIMED"              # read the message
$ fbmq ack /var/queue/jobs "$CLAIMED"

# Or on failure:
$ fbmq nack /var/queue/jobs "$CLAIMED"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 = success, 1 = empty queue (pop) or error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbmq-message (5),
.BR fbmq-design (7),
.BR rename (2),
.BR inotifywait (1)
